  "id": "chronometry",
  "term": "chronometry",
  "definition": "Chronometry, in this context also called mental chronometry, is the study of the timing of cognitive processes. It uses measures such as event-related potentials from EEG to estimate when mental processing occurs with very fine time resolution.",
